Package: easyDR
Title: Dose-Response Meta-Analysis, Made Teachable
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Vanio", "Antunes", email = "vanio.antunes.md@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Helpers for conducting and reporting dose-response
    meta-analyses, built alongside the companion book at
    <https://vanioljantunes.github.io/easyDR/>. The package wraps the
    steps that students repeatedly get wrong: checking whether a set of
    studies can support a dose-response model at all, and naming the
    shape of a fitted curve. Modelling itself is delegated to
    'dosresmeta'.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Depends: 
    R (>= 4.1)
Suggests: 
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    dosresmeta
Config/testthat/edition: 3
URL: https://github.com/vanioljantunes/easyDR, https://vanioljantunes.github.io/easyDR/
